{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"Select-String -Path SPEC.md,sim.py,bayes.py,latent_filter.py,e12_unlabelled_head.py,e13_rungs_over_time.py -Pattern '\"'^## E(12|13|14)|''^def |''^class |''^(T|RHO|HORIZON|THRESHOLD|PARAMETER_NAMES|N_PER_WEEK|WEEKS|SIGMA|ROOT|POLICY_NAMES|TRAIN|TEST|STREAM)'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"\r\nSPEC.md:34:Tests (pytest-free plain asserts in `test_sim_bayes.py`, runnable with numpy only):\r\nSPEC.md:49:Training: Adam lr 1e-3, weight decay 0, batch 256, BCE loss, max 120 epochs, early stopping on validation \r\nBCE (validation drawn under the TRAINING policy), patience 12, keep best checkpoint. Inputs computed once as tensors.\r\nSPEC.md:153:Ties in run-in loss (e.g. a run-in without cases) are broken towards w = 1.\r\nSPEC.md:196:## E12: re-learning the testing head at B without outcomes (Claude and Wesley, 23 Oct 2026; exploratory, \r\nquick version)\r\nSPEC.md:202:Target policies at B (sigma 1, rate 0.3 unless stated): `B_less` informative gamma 1 (less selective); \r\n`B_more` informative gamma 3.5 (more selective; the dial in [0, 1] cannot help here, see docs/GAP.md \"The dial above \r\n1\"); `B_match` uniform 0.3; `B_dense` uniform 0.6.\r\nSPEC.md:220:## E13: which rung when? Performance over weeks of deployment (Claude and Wesley, 23 Oct 2026; simulation)\r\nSPEC.md:235:Time axis: weeks t = 1, 2, 4, 8, 13, 26, 52, 104; 25 admissions per week (1,300 a year, a median US ICU), \r\nso n(t) = 25 t patients (about 0.5 outcome cases a week). All n(t) patients' testing records are available for R1; \r\ntheir outcomes are available for R2, R4 and `dial_only` (outcome delay ignored: the 6-hour horizon is short against a \r\nweek).\r\nSPEC.md:245:## E14: a shift only outcomes can reveal (Claude and Wesley, 25 Oct 2026; simulation, quick version)\r\nSPEC.md:251:Two directions:\r\nsim.py:10:T = 48\r\nsim.py:11